findings.what:
app/about.tsx:101 links https://kappsa.tech/Privacy-Policy/. Re-read live on 2026-11-11 ("Last updated: 16.06.2026"). It now names "Tinnitus Tracker" (the October "TinnitusTrack" point is fixed) but still:
- says the app collects Age (section 02 "Age"; section 12 "your name, age, tinnitus intensity, pitch") — nothing collects age (onboarding asks only a name, app/onboarding/name.tsx);
- says "The App uses Google AdMob to display advertisements" (section 11; section 05 lists Google AdMob) — no ads SDK is installed (package.json);
- describes accounts and sync (section 15: "Email address (if you create an account)", "Synchronize data across your devices", "request deletion of your account") — there are no accounts and no sync, and section 04 says everything is stored locally;
- names only Firebase, Google Analytics for Firebase, RevenueCat and AdMob; omits Crashlytics (app/utils/crashlytics.ts), Performance Monitoring by name (app/utils/performance.ts) and EAS Updates, which contacts u.expo.dev on every launch (app.json updates.url). Remote Config was removed from the app on 2026-10-17, so it no longer needs to be listed;
- does not describe the in-app opt-in for usage/crash data or the Settings › Privacy switch (section 07 lists only view / export / uninstall; section 15 says withdraw consent by email);
- states "not intended for children under the age of 13" while the Terms require users to be at least 16.
The October point about uninstalling not removing data no longer applies: android.allowBackup is false since PR #8, so "Uninstalling the App will permanently remove all data … from your device" is now true.
